add('4.2-02','Calculate the amount concentration of a solution containing 0.0100 mol solute in a total volume of 25.0 cm³. Show the volume conversion in your working.','V=25.0/1000=0.0250 dm³. c=n/V=0.0100/0.0250=0.400 mol/dm³. Treating 25 cm³ as 25 dm³ makes the answer 1000 times too small.',['0.0250 dm³ conversion (1).','c=n/V with corrected volume (1).','0.400 mol/dm³ (1); diagnostic explanation confirms the same unit correction rather than earning an extra mark.'])
