add('4.2-02','Calculate the NaCl mass formed on mixing 20.0 cm³ of 0.100 mol/dm³ HCl with 25.0 cm³ of 0.100 mol/dm³ NaOH. HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H2O. M(NaCl)=58.5 g/mol. Identify the limiting reactant in your working.','n(HCl)=0.100×0.0200=0.00200 mol; n(NaOH)=0.100×0.0250=0.00250 mol. HCl limits the 1:1 reaction. n(NaCl)=0.00200 mol; mass=0.00200×58.5=0.117 g.',['Both reacting amounts correct (1).','HCl limiting with 0.00200 mol salt (1).','0.117 g NaCl (1).'])
